# Variables for the gateway.
#
# On Railway: set these in the service's Variables tab. Railway reads this file
# and offers to import the names; fill in the two keys there.
# Locally: copy this file to .env, fill in the two keys, then run
#   node --env-file=.env src/server.js
#
# The two keys are left empty on purpose. The gateway refuses to start until
# both are set, so it can never come up unprotected or with a made-up key.

# Required. Your Mistral API key, from https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys
# It stays on the server and is never sent to callers.
MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# Required. The key your own apps send to this gateway. Make one up; do not
# reuse the Mistral key. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# Several keys can be given, separated by commas.
GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# The Mistral model this endpoint serves. See "Model retirement" in the README.
MISTRAL_MODEL=mistral-large-2512

# Optional. Leave these out unless you have a reason to change them.
# MISTRAL_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# PORT=8080
